# is non-empty, verifies its sha256 before executing it. Upstream rotates the
# script without notice, so empty = skip verification (the default). To pin
# deliberately: download, review, then record the hash:
#   curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://sh.rustup.rs | sha256sum
# noforward
# Rotated 2026-09-01 (rustup-init 1.29.0 -> 1.29.1). Verified before bumping:
# the script sh.rustup.rs serves is byte-identical to rust-lang/rustup's own
# rustup-init.sh except for ONE line, the version banner (929/930 lines match).
# Re-do that comparison on the next rotation; never bump this on 'it looks ok'.
RUSTUP_INIT_SHA256=7d0ea0f8eba7fa1ebfe998091cd7ec4501e33ec5ca6b884eb4d894d7da5170af
# Same optional pin for the uv installer executed by 01-core/python_uv.sh
# (uv_ensure_installed). Empty = skip (upstream rotates the script with each
# uv release):
#   curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://astral.sh/uv/install.sh | sha256sum
# noforward
UV_INSTALL_SH_SHA256=b8e6c43099ee9f9a550984d3ad56948457c689e7a99c090b35377234ac241491

# --- Flutter web: sqlite3.wasm ---
# drift/sqlite3.dart ships the WASM build as a release asset, and a Flutter web
# app that uses sqlite cannot start without it. Two consumers had copied the
# same 16-line fetcher and already disagreed on the version (OmniAccelerANT
# 3.3.1, jotrockenmitlocken 3.2.0), and NEITHER verified what it downloaded --
# an unauthenticated binary that then runs in every visitor's browser. The
# newer of the two is pinned here; the SHA256 is of the asset itself, measured
# 2026-09-08. Consumer entry point:
# linux/scripts/05-frameworks/flutter/setup-sqlite3-wasm.sh <consumer-root>
SQLITE3_WASM_VERSION=3.3.1
SQLITE3_WASM_SHA256=3c616bf0d51380daaed7871b3110a634a17c703c22d82cba7a2a73216769e680

# --- WebDavClient -----------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's own WebDAV client, installed from git (it is not on PyPI) by both
# halves of the downloader: 01-core/webdav-download.sh on Linux and
# WindowsWebDav.Common.psm1 on Windows. Pinned because an unpinned
# `git+https://.../WebDavClient` installs whatever the default branch was that
# day, which makes "which client did this run use" unanswerable -- and one
# consumer had already pinned it privately while the hub's two call sites had
# not, so the three could disagree. This is the commit that consumer pinned.
WEBDAVCLIENT_REF=4f3f116d9ce7d1e223894513b4dc7a90b5085a9f
